\begin_layout Subsection
Clustering
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
K-means is a method for cluster analysis.
 It consists in building a partition of 
\begin_inset Formula $n$
\end_inset

 observations into 
\begin_inset Formula $k$
\end_inset

 clusters in which each observation belongs to the cluster with the nearest mean,
 serving as a prototype of the cluster.
 In the case of a grayscale image,
 this results in a muti-level threshold based on images intensities.
 In the case of a multi-variate image,
 each observation corresponds to an image element,
 and each component corresponds a feature.
 The resulting clusters correspond to groups of pixels with similar or near colors or channel intensities.
\end_layout

